    week: 5,
    term: "Third_Term",
    session: "2025/2026",
    content: "1.\tThe objective question options are not displaying at the student’s portal. There are no options to choose from the objective questions.\n2.\tWhen a student finish taking CBT Exams/assignment/homework, let the system automatically marks and score the exercise, display and save result for the students. \n3.\tWhen a student finish taking CBT Exams/assignment/homework, let the system automatically notifies the teacher in the “teacher’s portal” to mark the theory questions if there is any, if there is none let the system send and save “result score sheet” containing scores and details of all the students that wrote the CBT Exams/assignment/homework. \n4.\tWhen a user performs any action, the displayed notification message for that action should disappear after 25 seconds. Like when a add question in the CBT exams generator it does not go away till after refreshing the browser.\n5.\tAt the “Apply for admission”, add the following features/functions/pages/portal, “do not delete or remove the forms already built in there”:\n•\tWhen a user clicks on “apply for admission” button, the “requirements/instructions” page opens first.\n•\tThe user chooses a section and the class intended for then the “requirements/instructions” for that particular class is displayed, the user reads, accepts and agrees before proceeding to fill the admission form. \n\n“REQUIREMENTS/INSTRUCTIONS” feature/function/contents;\nA.\tPre-Nursey to Nursery Two\n“New intake (Compulsory fees)”\nTuition fee = 15, 000\nAdmission form = 2, 000\nExamination fee = 1, 000\nRegistration = 2, 000\nP.T.A Levy = 500\nLesson fee = 1, 000\nBadges = 500 \n\nTotal = 22, 000\nSubsequently = 17, 500\n\n“New Intake (Compulsory Items)”\n1.\tTwo office files\n2.\tTwo Passport\n3.\tTwo antiseptic Soaps\n4.\tTwo toilet paper\n5.\tOne Izal/Bleach (small size)\n6.\tOne Dettol\n7.\tDetergent (Omo) \n\nB.\tPrimary 1 to Primary 5\n“New intake (Compulsory fees)”\nTuition fee = 18, 500\nAdmission form = 2, 000\nExamination fee = 1, 000\nRegistration = 2, 000\nP.T.A Levy = 500\nLesson fee = 1, 000\nBadges = 500 \n\nTotal = 25, 500\nSubsequently = 21, 000\n\n“New Intake (Compulsory Items)”\n1.\tTwo office files\n2.\tTwo Passport\n3.\tTwo antiseptic Soaps\n4.\tTwo toilet paper\n5.\tOne Izal/Bleach (small size)\n6.\tOne Dettol\n7.\tDetergent (Omo) \n\nC.\tJSS1 to JSS3\n“New intake (Compulsory fees)”\nTuition fee = 30, 500\nAdmission form = 2, 000\nExamination fee = 1, 000\nRegistration = 2, 000\nP.T.A Levy = 1,000\nLesson fee = 1, 000\nBadges = 500\nPractical fee = 1, 000\nMedical fee = 1, 000 \n\nTotal = 40, 000\nSubsequently = 33, 000\n\n“New Intake (Compulsory Items)”\n1.\tTwo office files\n2.\tTwo Passport\n3.\tTwo hoes\n4.\tTwo brooms\n5.\tTwo cutlasses \n6.\tTwo antiseptic Soaps\n7.\tTwo toilet paper\n8.\tOne Izal/Bleach (small size)\n9.\tOne Dettol\n\nD.\tSS1 to SS3\n“New intake (Compulsory fees)”\nTuition fee = 36, 500\nAdmission form = 2, 000\nExamination fee = 1, 000\nRegistration = 2, 000\nP.T.A Levy = 1,000\nLesson fee = 1, 000\nBadges = 500\nPractical fee = 1, 000\nMedical fee = 1, 000 \n\nTotal = 46, 000\nSubsequently = 39, 000\n\n“New Intake (Compulsory Items)”\n1.\tTwo office files\n2.\tTwo Passport\n3.\tTwo hoes\n4.\tTwo brooms\n5.\tTwo cutlasses \n6.\tTwo antiseptic Soaps\n7.\tTwo toilet paper\n8.\tOne Izal/Bleach (small size)\n9.\tOne Dettol\n•\t After the above steps then a user accepts then proceeds to apply for admission by filling the information in the different steps of forms as required for admission.\n•\tLet the system automatically sends a copy of the application form to the user with their unique application number after submission.   \n•\tLet the system automatically generates a unique and different application number for any user at the application submission.  \n•\tAccountant gets a notification then reviews the application then accepts or rejects the application.  \n•\tIf a user is offered admission, a congratulatory message is displayed with two options (reject or accept admission). If a user accepts the admission, the system automatically sends an acceptance letter to the user email for printing and bringing it to the school.\n•\tLet the system automatically generates an admission number (follow the admission number pattern already existing in the database), add it to the acceptance letter and sent to the user email.\n•\t Acceptance letter contains instructions such as 1. The @user is require come to the school for academic testing of the class applied for. 2. This acceptance letter does not any anyway connote that the @user is admitted into the desired class until test is conducted. \n•\tA user can check their admission status (by inputting their application number).\n•\tAfter a physical testing, accountant enters the user’s application number, test score and class to be admitted into, then the system automatically generates an admission letter and send it to the user email and also make it ready to be print by the accountant.\n•\tLet the system extracts the user’s admission number and information from the application form and store and save permanently in the database after admission letter is sent to the email.\n",
